_margin": 10.0, "analyst_adjustment": 0.0, "key_factors": ["Washington's D+10 partisan lean and decades-long Democratic presidential streak", "Open race: the term-limited incumbent gives neither party an incumbency edge", "No state polls, expert ratings, or market pricing yet; fundamentals carry the estimate", "2028 nominee choices and the national environment could shift the margin"], "rationale": "Washington's durable Democratic lean at the presidential level, with no incumbent on the ballot to offset it, points to a Democratic win of roughly ten points; with no polls, ratings, or market pricing available, there is no specific evidence to move from that fundamentals-based starting point.", "watch": "The identity of each party's nominee and the national political climate could move Washington's margin well off its partisan lean.", "confidence": "medium", "notes": ["No expert ratings published yet; forecast rests on fundamentals and polls.", "New or vacant seat with no expert ratings; fundamentals only.", "No usable general-election polls; forecast rests on fundamentals and expert ratings."]}, "overview": "Washington has voted Democratic in every presidential election for more than three decades, and its partisan lean sits around ten points Democratic. With a term-limited incumbent leaving the ballot, neither party carries an incumbency advantage, so the race starts from the state's underlying lean. No candidate-level polling, expert ratings, or market pricing is available for this race yet, and campaign money is not yet reported.\n\nWith no direct evidence, expectations rest on fundamentals: a Democratic edge of roughly ten points, with uncertainty wide enough to reflect the absence of polling. Headlines so far concern the parties' 2028 nomination contests rather than Washington itself, and no development in them clearly favors one side in this state. A Democratic win is more likely than not, but the margin could move meaningfully once nominees are chosen and polling arrives.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.873, "margin": 10.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.8189, "margin": 10.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.8232, "margin": 10.0}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.8205, "margin": 10.0}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.826, "margin": 10.0}]}